{"reference":"John 11","book":"John","chapter":11,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"chapter_overview","title":"Overview","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The Lazarus narrative holds friendship, delay, grief, belief, glory, death, and a life-giving sign together rather than treating them as competing themes. Jesus’ tears therefore do not present grief as a spiritual failure; they belong within a story that also moves toward Lazarus’s return from the tomb and the political escalation that follows.","verse_refs":["John 11:1-57","John 11:25-26","John 11:45-53"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_john_011_bcac2b7969358e54cbca2e6d"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"The council and Caiaphas","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"The council scene should not be read as though every priestly or council figure held the same role. The chapter names chief priests, Pharisees, and Caiaphas as high priest, while related accounts distinguish further Jerusalem offices and groups. Evidence also indicates that high priests could retain substantial local influence while operating within Roman and client-royal power. This helps clarify why the leaders frame Jesus’ growing following as a threat to both their place and their nation.","verse_refs":["John 11:47-53"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_john_011_eb2bde93fac6cddc83b63737"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"},{"id":"block_3","text":"Caiaphas argues that one person should die for the people rather than the whole nation perish. The narration then gives his words a second meaning: his political calculation is presented as an unintended prophecy. The irony does not approve scapegoating; it exposes the gap between Caiaphas’s immediate reasoning and the meaning the narrator finds in his statement.","verse_refs":["John 11:1-57","John 11:25-26","John 11:45-53"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_john_011_bcac2b7969358e54cbca2e6d"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}